WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:03.069
We don't always
have enough time to cover all

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.538
of the recent news,
so, here, with a recap is

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:08.274
"Late Night" writer Amber Ruffin
in a segment we call

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.542
"Amber Says What."

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:11.444
♪♪

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:14.247
-You guys,
things have been crazy!

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:17.317
Okay, first of all, I found out
that there isn't gonna be

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.619
a big, fat
Emmy ceremony this year.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.187
And I was like, "What?!"

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:24.257
They were like, "We are still
not gathering in large groups."

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:25.291
And I was like, "What?!"

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.725
I miss people!

00:00:26.725 --> 00:00:28.527
Then, they were like,
"This is good for you, Amber,

00:00:28.527 --> 00:00:30.597
because you're not gonna
be able to get drunk

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.431
and act a fool
in a formal gown."

00:00:32.431 --> 00:00:34.400
And I was like, "What?!

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.835
You can't tell me what to do."

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:41.040
Then, Donald Trump bragged
about passing a cognitive test

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.408
and I was like, "What?!"

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:44.810
Do you think they give
those to everybody?

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.213
They give them to people
who are losing their dang minds.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:50.049
This is like you bragging
you took a sobriety test.

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:51.918
If you weren't swerving
all over the place,

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:54.153
you wouldn't have to identify
shapes and animals.

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:56.156
Tsk.
You wanna impress me?

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:57.924
Spell cognitive.

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.124
The test is too easy.

00:00:59.124 --> 00:01:01.260
Look, I'll take it right now.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:02.294
Idiot.

00:01:02.294 --> 00:01:03.563
I passed!

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:06.065
Then, a megachurch pastor
in Atlanta suggested that,

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:07.967
instead of saying
white privilege,

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:10.069
that people should say
white blessing

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:11.938
and I was like, "What?!"

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:13.406
White blessing?!

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:16.109
You mean my nickname
for Anderson Cooper?

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.477
White blessing?!

00:01:17.477 --> 00:01:19.846
You mean the stripper
from Tina's bachelorette party?

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.213
White blessing?!

00:01:21.213 --> 00:01:24.416
Sounds like the nastiest
sex move.

00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:26.619
Then, I read a story
about how a Black man

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:29.655
carried a Black Lives Matter
counterprotester to safety

00:01:29.655 --> 00:01:31.157
and I was like, "What?!"

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.658
But the makers
of "The Green Book"

00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:33.793
were like, "What?!

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.295
We had better get
to writing this story

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:38.097
from the perspective
of the man who was carried!"

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:39.833
You know what they're gonna
call that movie, don't you?

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.102
Then, I found out there
was gonna be

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:45.471
a professional
women's soccer team

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:46.839
in Los Angeles,

00:01:46.839 --> 00:01:49.875
with Serena Williams
and Natalie Portman as investors

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:51.243
and I was like, "What?!

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:52.311
Hurray!"

00:01:52.311 --> 00:01:53.813
I'm gonna find out
when auditions are

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.982
and prepare
a dramatic monologue.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:58.851
Then, my friend told me it's
not auditions, it's tryouts,

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:01.254
and you don't prepare
a monologue. You play the sport.

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:02.988
And I was like,
"Okay, fine, but,

00:02:02.988 --> 00:02:05.725
I'm still gonna wear a gown."

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:08.928
Speaking of sports,
I found out about the NBA bubble

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.129
and I was like, "What?!"

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:13.666
Because -- and the thing
about the NBA bubble is

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:17.169
it's a metaphorical bubble
in a physical --

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:19.038
-Amber, you don't have
to talk about that.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:20.339
-Yay!

00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:22.675
Then, I saw that people
are circulating a petition

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:26.012
to replace Confederate statues
with statues of Dolly Parton

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:27.847
and I was like, "What?!"

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:31.116
Now, that's what I call
a white-centered solution.

00:02:31.116 --> 00:02:33.519
No shade to Dolly, but,
if slave owners get replaced

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:35.754
with anything less Black
than Malcolm X,

00:02:35.754 --> 00:02:37.723
I will freak the [bleep] out.

00:02:37.723 --> 00:02:40.059
Then, Ivanka Trump was like,
"Eat these beans!"

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:41.694
And I was like, "What?! No!"

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:44.163
Then, Obama
and Joe Biden sat down

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:46.365
for a socially distanced
conversation

00:02:46.365 --> 00:02:48.133
and I was like, "What

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:51.470
are you doing, sitting so far
away from each other?"

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:53.305
Is it six feet or sixty feet?

00:02:53.305 --> 00:02:56.608
Obama, are you trying
to distance yourself from Biden?

00:02:56.608 --> 00:02:59.645
That's not gonna work 'cause he
mentions you in every sentence.

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:02.881
Then, infectious disease
expert Dr. Anthony Fauci

00:03:02.881 --> 00:03:04.183
threw out the first pitch

00:03:04.183 --> 00:03:06.352
at the Washington Nationals'
Opening Day

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.920
and I was like, "What

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.722
are you doing playing catch?!"

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:12.525
You had better get inside
and take care of America!

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.860
I'm walking around
with a cut-up sock on my face

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.495
and you are at recess?

00:03:16.495 --> 00:03:18.798
Get inside and do something!

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.566
Then, I saw the pitch
and felt better

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:23.836
because it was clear he didn't
waste any time practicing.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:26.105
Then, Marco Rubio posted
a picture of him

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:27.707
and the late
Congressman John Lewis,

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.842
but it was actually
a picture of him

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:31.711
and the late
Congressman Elijah Cummings

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.880
and I was like, "What?!"

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.882
Do you think that all
of us look alike?

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:38.551
By "us," I mean, people
who don't like you.

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.252
Then, I heard
that Jennifer Hudson

00:03:40.252 --> 00:03:42.722
is gonna play Aretha Franklin
in a new biopic

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:43.990
and I was like --
[ Gasp ]

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.625
♪ Just a little what,
just a little what ♪

00:03:46.625 --> 00:03:48.394
♪ What it to me, what it to me,
what it to me, what it to me ♪

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:50.996
Then, the most confusing thing
in the world happened.

00:03:50.996 --> 00:03:52.898
Okay, Trump was gonna
give a speech

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:54.901
and he had these
two trucks there,

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.668
a blue one with a bunch
of weight in the bed

00:03:56.668 --> 00:03:57.804
and a sign that said...

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:01.708
...and then, a red one,
with no weights, that said...

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:05.444
I guess it was supposed
to represent

00:04:05.444 --> 00:04:07.379
how free Republicans are.

00:04:07.379 --> 00:04:09.048
Look, I think it's nuts

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:10.883
and it brings us
to a segment called

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.051
"Amber Says Why."

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:13.819
♪♪

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:15.120
You wanted to make some point

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:17.022
about how regulations
weigh you down

00:04:17.022 --> 00:04:18.991
and this is how
you chose to do it?"

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:20.192
Why?

00:04:20.192 --> 00:04:21.560
Why this?

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:24.730
Why did someone do this and what
is the this that they did?

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:27.467
What's the point of this,
to prove it could be done?

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:28.534
Why?

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.102
Why did someone do this?

00:04:30.102 --> 00:04:31.770
What was the desired effect?

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:34.039
Laughter, pride, shame, what?

00:04:34.039 --> 00:04:35.874
What is this, a dare?!

00:04:35.874 --> 00:04:37.209
What? Why?!

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:39.812
Why is this happening
and what is what is happening?

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:42.582
Why this?
This, why?!

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:44.984
Why did this happen
and why did you let someone

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:47.119
take pictures of it
while it was happening?

00:04:47.119 --> 00:04:48.988
Did you know
this was gonna be public?

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.489
Was it meant to be private?

00:04:50.489 --> 00:04:52.324
Did you know
that people can see this?

00:04:52.324 --> 00:04:53.825
I can see this!

00:04:53.825 --> 00:04:55.627
Where did this idea come from,

00:04:55.627 --> 00:04:56.929
a dream, a threat?

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:58.064
Where?!

00:04:58.064 --> 00:04:59.665
Did this happen
against your will

00:04:59.665 --> 00:05:01.700
or was this exactly
what you wanted?

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:04.236
And, if so, why is this
a want that you have?

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:05.570
[ Clapping ]
Why are your wants bad?

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.640
Don't you want good?
Why?!

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.109
Did a dumb person tell you
this was not dumb or --

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:11.677
and this is
what I think happened --

00:05:11.677 --> 00:05:14.747
did a smart person who hates you
tell you this was not dumb?

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:15.982
Who lied?!

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:17.150
How many people had to lie

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:20.019
for this to take place,
one, 100?

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:22.255
Did you think that this was
what someone wanted done

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:25.491
and who are they
and are they okay?

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:28.193
In closing, why?!

00:05:28.193 --> 00:05:32.164
This has been "Amber Says What
&amp; Then She Says Why."

00:05:32.164 --> 00:05:33.466
♪♪

